s if the left side is True).\",\n20:     \"//\": \"`//` is floor division: it divides and rounds down to the nearest whole integer.\",\n21:     \"+=\": \"`+=` adds the right-hand value to the variable on the left and stores the new total back in that variable.\",\n22:     \"-=\": \"`-=` subtracts the right-hand value from the variable on the left and updates it.\",\n23:     \">=\": \"`>=` tests whether the left value is greater than or equal to the right value (`True` or `False`).\",\n24:     \"<=\": \"`<=` tests whether the left value is less than or equal to the right value (`True` or `False`).\",\n25:     \"==\": \"`==` compares two values for equality (`True` if equal, `False` otherwise).\",\n26:     \"!=\": \"`!=` checks whether two values are different (`True` if not equal).\",\n27:     \"<\": \"`<` checks if the left value is strictly smaller than the right value.\",\n28:     \">\": \"`>` checks if the left value is strictly larger than the right value.\",\n29:     \"=\": \"`=` is the assignment operator: it calculates the right side first and binds the variable name to that object's memory address.\",\n30:     \"[]\": \"Square brackets `[i]` access the element at index position `i` inside a list (starting at index `0`).\",\n31:     \"->\": \"`->` is a type hint showing what data type the function is expected to return.\",\n32: }\n33: \n34: \n35: def explain_symbols_in_line(code_text: str) -> str:\n36:     found = []\n37:     for sym, desc in PYTHON_SYMBOL_DICTIONARY.items():\n38:         if sym in code_text:\n39:             found.append(f\"• {desc}\")\n40:     if not found:\n41:         return \"• Standard Python expression evaluation.\"\n42:     return \"\\n\".join(found[:3])\n43: \n44: \n45: def generate_step_explanation(step: Dict[str, Any], prev_step: Dict[str, Any] = None) -> Dict[str, str]:\n46:     \"\"\"\n47:     Produces beginner and technical explanations from a recorded execution step,\n48:     incorporating sub-expression evaluation frames and memory reference details.\n49:     \"\"\"\n50:     code = step.get(\"codeText\", \"\").strip()\n51:     event = step.get(\"event\", \"line\")\n52:     cond = step.get(\"condition\")\n53:     op_detail = step.get(\"operationDetail\")\n54:     changed = step.get(\"changedSummary\", \"No variable values changed\")\n55:     before_vars = step.get(\"beforeVars\", {})\n56:     expr_frames = step.get(\"exprFrames\", [])\n57: \n58:     short_circuit_frame = next((f for f in expr_frames if f.get(\"shortCircuited\")), None)\n59: \n60:     if code.startswith(\"class \"):\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
